From: SF2000 Linux <sf2000@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] qpsx: force the XLOG load trace on for on-device stall diagnosis

The SF2000 Linux core keeps its firmware debug logging off by default so
the no-FPU machine is not slowed.  While diagnosing the on-device
retro_load_game() stall (works under QEMU, hangs on hardware) the XLOG
trace must be active so the kmsg-routed adapter (xlog -> /dev/kmsg) shows
exactly which load step never returns.

qpsx_apply_config() calls update_debug_log_state() with the config value
(default off) during retro_load_game(), which would reset the trace off
again, so the switch is forced on there as well.

TEMPORARY: remove this patch from MUFROG_qpsx_PATCHES once the stall is
fixed; the core then returns to g_debug_log_enabled = 0.

--- a/libretro/core/libretro-core.cpp
+++ b/libretro/core/libretro-core.cpp
@@ -72,2 +72,3 @@
 /* Global flag for debug logging (set from qpsx_config.debug_log) */
-static int g_debug_log_enabled = 0;
+/* SF2000 Linux diagnostic: keep the load trace on until the stall is fixed. */
+static int g_debug_log_enabled = 1;
@@ -100,3 +100,5 @@
 static void update_debug_log_state(int enabled)
 {
-    g_debug_log_enabled = enabled;
+    /* SF2000 Linux diagnostic: ignore the config and keep tracing on. */
+    (void)enabled;
+    g_debug_log_enabled = 1;
